Derived work: Mondrian
----------------------

olap4abap is in large part a port to ABAP of Mondrian, the OLAP server (https://github.com/pentaho/mondrian), in
version 9.3 of Sergei Semenkov's eMondrian fork (https://github.com/SergeiSemenkov/mondrian, branch eMondrian, and
https://github.com/SergeiSemenkov/eMondrian). The ported parts are the MDX parser
(from the JavaCC grammar MdxParser.jj), the validator, the built-in function table, the evaluator and the functions,
the format strings, the schema definition (MondrianDef), the XMLA rowsets and answers, and the error texts. Mondrian
is distributed under the Eclipse Public License 1.0, and the ported code is distributed here under the Eclipse Public
License 2.0 as section 7 of the EPL 1.0 allows. Its copyright notices:

  Copyright (C) 1998-2005 Julian Hyde
  Copyright (C) 2005-2021 Hitachi Vantara and others
  Copyright (C) 2021-2025 Sergei Semenkov

The source code of Mondrian is available at the addresses above; scripts/setup-reference.sh fetches the version this
port follows. scripts/patches/ holds our changes to it, under the license of the files they change (EPL 1.0).

Mondrian is a trademark of Hitachi Vantara. olap4abap is not affiliated with or endorsed by Hitachi Vantara.

The test data (tests/, reference/ and the unit tests) holds MDX statements of Mondrian's test suite and its demo
schemas FoodMart.xml and SteelWheels.xml (Eclipse Public License 1.0), answers captured from the eMondrian server, and
the schema Foodmart.xml of the eMondrian web application (https://github.com/SergeiSemenkov/eMondrian, Apache License
2.0, http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).


